      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims an ecosystemic approach involves “all responsible parties rather than focusing on just one individual,” but the packet only states “utilize an ecosystemic approach involving all responsible parties” without specifying a contrast with focusing on one individual.",
        "The definition says the approach “include[s] the wider people and systems connected to the situation,” but the packet does not mention “systems” or “wider people” beyond the phrase “all responsible parties.”",
        "Although the packet supports that interventions should “consider their subtypes” (i.e., bullying subtypes), the definition adds additional wording (about wider systems and contrasting against individual-only focus) that is not supported by the provided text."
